MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The burr sets feel like useful next steps after drilling, cutting and fastening: they could help me smooth edges and shape parts for the same workshop projects.",
    "Lag bolts, repair tape, wire connectors and magnetic hooks fit my pattern of keeping practical repair supplies and organizing tools available, with the larger wood fasteners adding something beyond my smaller screw assortments."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "The anatomy model has no connection to the workshop tasks I am doing; I have shown no need for medical study or teaching equipment.",
    "The sprayer nozzles and pressure gauge require specific needs I have not shown. Owning dropper bottles does not mean I need replacement sprayers, and using calipers or a thermometer does not establish a pressure-testing project."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My interest in tools seems to have been stretched into an interest in specialized equipment without a clear use in my current projects.",
    "My repeated purchases of assortments seem to imply that I always need more bulk supplies, even when fifty identical screws or twenty-four sprayers would need a specific reason."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "Compatibility matters before I choose: the two burr sets have different shank sizes, and I would select the one that fits my equipment rather than buy both.",
    "My existing supplies affect what I need next. A larger fastener assortment could extend what I can do, while another specific screw size can wait until a project calls for it."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations recognize my practical workshop interests but sometimes mistake a related tool or supply for something I currently need."
}
